From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:43:35 +0800
Subject: app/composer: working timer next to the stop button, like pi's

While the agent works, the composer shows how long the current run has been
going ("17s", "2m 05s", "1h 03m") left of the stop/send button. It keeps
counting across steps, tool calls and queued follow-ups and clears when the
session goes idle.

The start time is session.execution.started's time, which the client data layer
now remembers per session (data.session.runStarted). A page opened mid-run falls
back to the last user message's time.

The shimmering "Working" row at the bottom of the timeline is removed: it only
showed when nothing else looked busy, so it kept appearing and disappearing.

Ocelot-Patch: web/working-timer

